{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Away.</b> From a distance." "<b>As a bowshot.</b> Like two shots (Bereshit Rabbah); and it is an expression of shooting an arrow — in the language of the Mishnah, 'who shot at his wife' — so named because the seed shoots forth like an arrow. And if you say, it should have written כִּמְטַחֵי קֶשֶׁת — the rule of the vav is to enter here, as in ״בְּחַגְוֵי הַסֶּלַע״ (Song of Songs 2), from the derivation of ״וְהָיְתָה אַדְמַת יְהוּדָה לְמִצְרַיִם לְחָגָּא״ (Isaiah 19), and from the derivation of ״יָחֹגּוּ וְיָנוּעוּ כַּשִּׁכּוֹר״ (Psalms 107); and likewise ״קַצְוֵי אֶרֶץ״ (Psalms 65) — from the derivation of קָצֶה." "<b>And she sat away.</b> Once he drew near to death, she distanced herself further."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:48.395695778Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}